From ed4096658dffa7ab796838db092f6ce66e025dc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jaytriana <83611075+jaytriana@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 18:38:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] 0001 CHOP: keep the sample list open on a SAMPLE
 double-tap; document the double-tap, note-off routing and first-flash order

A quick second SAMPLE press is stock's double-tap (bit2) and opens the sample
list without reaching sample_key_gate, but the arm byte from the first press was
still set at its release, so that release cycled the page back and the title
call closed the list. The release path now hands the event to the base cycle
only when no list popup is open (weak_ptr_expired(view+512)); otherwise stock.

Docs only otherwise: CHOP is reached by press, pause, press (a quick double-tap
stays stock's sample-list shortcut); turning CHP while a pad is held can send
that pad's note-off to another track (D8 as written; KeyboardView ignores
note-offs); a "Before you flash" block with the control -> chop-min -> chop
order, the recovery route and the verified .syx hashes; the new built addresses
(stub 872 -> 888 B).

make chop, chop-min, control, random and the default make all PASS in the guest;
the default .syx is byte-identical to before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mods/0001-chop/design.md | 151 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 mods/0001-chop/mod.toml  |  10 +--
 mods/0001-chop/stub.s    |  32 +++++++--
 3 files changed, 159 insertions(+), 34 deletions(-)

