Subject: [PATCH 5/7] 0001 CHOP: hold trig keys + pad = STA p-lock of that
 pad's marker on every held step

In CHOP, a pad hit with trig key(s) of the chop track held now does what stock
does when you hold those trigs and turn STA: each held step gets an STA p-lock
equal to the pad's marker (stock's own held-trig path: mark the hold edited so
the release does not toggle, visit the held steps, write through the sound
set's lock setter, clear the pending actions). The base STA is then left alone.
Without a held trig, with CHOP off, or with a held trig on another track, the
pad does exactly what it did before. Symbols for the stock routines added to
re/symbols.toml; design.md gains the proof and test card H6. make chop,
chop-min and control PASS in the guest; the stub is 1224 B of its 1232 B claim.

